  "limitations": [
    "Public benchmark only, isolated from user accounts. Country aggregates from one retailer are correlated, not independent shops. Gift/wholesale sales in 2010-2011 are a different task from fresh-product store sales in 2024; no direct numeric v1/v2 comparison, no claim that boosting generalized, no Indonesian pilot, no public-model activation or Qwen fine-tuning. After the first report this external test is known and repetition is reproducibility only.",
    "The method was retrained in the new domain; this does not test fixed FreshRetailNet weights.",
    "Gross positive published invoice units omit returns/cancellation reconciliation and latent demand. Aggregate zero means no matching published event, not proof of no real demand.",
    "No known stockout, weather, holiday or customer features. No personal customer identifiers copied to derived files.",
    "Raw-unit pooled errors can be dominated by the UK; normalized and equal-country summaries are also reported.",
    "Observed earlier holdout days enter later lags; no full-period recursive forecast or refitting after the external score."
  ]
